WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.910
If you want to see how the father could have
survived while still saving his kids, stick

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:10.210
around to the end of this video.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.480
So I checked out A Quiet Place again and noticed
some new Things You Missed that I wanted to

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:18.740
share with whoever is out there and still
alive and has a pair of headphones. But first

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.909
I wanted to address something from the last
video, which you should go here and watch

00:00:22.909 --> 00:00:27.839
before watching this video. I got soooo many
comments saying that the red lights were not

00:00:27.839 --> 00:00:31.910
meant to hurt the creatures, they were just
a sign to be on red alert, because of aliens

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.270
in the area or because the baby was being
born.

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:39.059
I totally agree. That is the purpose of the
red lights, and I didn't mean for it to come

00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:42.860
off in any other way. What I was saying was
that when the wife turns on the red lights,

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:46.700
there is an unmistakable high pitched sound
emmited from them. Go back and watch that

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.769
scene and you'll see what I mean. I don't
know if that is an intended side effect of

00:00:50.769 --> 00:00:54.490
having the red lights on or if it was just
a happy accident, but it does seem to throw

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:58.160
the monsters off a little bit by providing
the family with a long string of continuous

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.160
sound.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.629
Just as the river offered protection from
small noises, this, on an even quieter level,

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:07.759
may have afforded them a little leeway needed
to move around the house. But the other then

00:01:07.759 --> 00:01:11.100
the volume, another difference between the
river and the sting of red lights, is that

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:16.390
the sound coming from the lights is a much
higher frequency, and as we saw from the hearing

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:21.600
aid, an extremely high frequency sound can
hurt the monsters and make them vulnerable.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.189
So when I talked about the opening shot of
the movie, with the traffic lights taken down,

00:01:25.189 --> 00:01:28.829
I was just saying that could be a clue for
the audience, as to what the weakness might

00:01:28.829 --> 00:01:33.811
be. When watching the movie again, I noticed
perhaps when more evidence towards this. After

00:01:33.811 --> 00:01:37.259
the baby is born, when the father comes up
from the bunker to find the two older kids,

00:01:37.259 --> 00:01:40.890
the string lights are now ripped from the
ceiling and on the floor. The aliens didn't

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.360
really attack anything else in the house,
other than the water pipe, which may have

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:48.350
been inadvertent, like the pipe just happened
to intersect with where the lights were set

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:49.350
up.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:52.030
But like I said the main purpose of those
lights was a visual cue for everyone to be

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:56.659
on high alert, because obviously blasting
a siren or something wouldn't work in their

00:01:56.659 --> 00:01:57.659
favor.

00:01:57.659 --> 00:02:00.700
There was one other thing in the last video
that I got more evidence for the second time

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:05.030
around, which was my theory that the creatures
are in fact aliens. Remember, last time we

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:08.879
had this shot that was used in a trailer but
not the movie. This time I noticed a couple

00:02:08.879 --> 00:02:13.700
more headlines posted up in the father's basement
lab. The first read "meteorite hits Mexico"

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.540
which gives us a clue about where and how
the epidemic started. If you were wondering

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:22.050
where A Quiet Place takes place, there's a
newspaper stand in town that says Little Falls,

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:26.070
NY. So the family we see in the movie had
some time to prepare before the aliens made

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.700
their way across North America to get to them.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:33.310
There was another headline I caught that was
way in the background, and partially cut off

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:38.769
screen. I saw the letters A L I E... So I'm
assuming that says Aliens, and I think we've

00:02:38.769 --> 00:02:44.030
got enough to confirm now that these creatures
are extra terrestrials. My question is, what

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:48.210
did the father do before the apocalypse, that
left him so well prepared? I think it's likely

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:52.300
he was some kind of telecommunications expert,
because of all the equipment he has, but he

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:56.401
also sets up his own video surveillance, and
has a printed list of every country. Keep

00:02:56.401 --> 00:03:00.980
in mind, he would have had to have that printed
before the invasion started, because printers

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:01.980
are loud.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.730
So what do you think he did before the takeover?
And why didn't he want his daughter going

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:09.049
into the basement? Leave your ideas in the
comments.

00:03:09.049 --> 00:03:12.580
One thing you may or may not have noticed
early on that certainly went past me was the

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:16.500
seriousness of the opening scene. The family
goes to a drug store to get pills for the

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:20.880
older son, who is sick. It's pretty scary
to think that even a simple cough could be

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.599
deadly in this world because of the noise.
Minor congestion could lead to snoring, which

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:30.989
could also be dangerous. That why the father
has medical supplies written on his whiteboard,

00:03:30.989 --> 00:03:33.340
staying healthy becomes extremely important.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:37.049
I'm guessing they go into town for supplies
fairly often, because the father actually

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:41.409
lays down a sand path all the way down into
town to quiet their footsteps.

00:03:41.409 --> 00:03:44.480
There were a couple of other things I noticed
that they did to keep things quiet, like painting

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:47.810
the floorboards that don't creek a slightly
different color.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:51.560
Someone else in the comments talked about
the reason that the hearing aid bugs out around

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:56.020
the aliens. I had previously said it could
be because of a feedback loop, but this person

00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:00.380
suggested that the aliens might give off some
kind of electromagnetic waves that mess with

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:05.000
electronics. There seems to be even more evidence
for this. When the wife goes into labor, a

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.069
lightbulb above the bath flickers as the alien
comes up the stairs. We see the same thing

00:04:09.069 --> 00:04:13.760
happen in the basement to a smaller lamp,
and when the monster goes down near the surveillance

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:18.220
screens, they all turn to static. After the
creature is killed, they return to normal.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:22.160
I did pick up something very interesting in
the early going about the younger son. It

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:27.630
almost seems like he doesn't have the will
to live quietly. Kids are always loud an obnoxious,

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:31.940
and maybe they need to get that energy out
by making noise. He draws a rocket ship on

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:36.580
the floor of the drug store and tells his
sister "that's how we get away." Then he intentionally

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:41.220
put in the batteries and turns on the rocket
on the bridge. So he essentially uses the

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:46.140
rocket to get away from this life that he
hates. That's a dark way of looking at it,

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.780
but after seeing it again, it does look to
be intentional. I thought it was strange that

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:54.290
they let the kid trail behind the pack like
that. I mean if he were to have wandered off,

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:58.530
they would likely never find him. They wouldn't
be able to call out how name when they went

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:03.400
searching for him, which would make it pretty
much impossible. I would have kept the kid

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:07.050
in front. And towards the end of the movie,
there was something I would have done differently

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:11.880
as well. The dad's last action to save his
kids was to yell out and distract the alien

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:16.200
trying to get into the car that the kids are
hiding in. Moments before, he grabs an axe

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:20.390
from the toolshed and tries to fight the creature
off, which doesn't work. I think all he had

00:05:20.390 --> 00:05:25.450
to do was throw that axe back into the toolshed
and aim to knock over some stuff in there.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.690
That should have afforded them some time to
flee.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:32.540
The other thing I thought about was the fact
that the baby is born on Day 473, and comes

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:38.400
about 2 weeks early. That means the baby must
have been concieved around day 259, almost

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.850
a year into the invasion. So what does that
mean? Aside from probably some really boring

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:48.941
quiet sex, it means they intentionally brought
a child into this world, most likely to try

00:05:48.941 --> 00:05:52.160
to do whatever they could to prevent mankind
from dying out.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:56.290
There may actually be some religious symbolism
to match the themes of perpetuating man. The

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:59.880
first being that the baby is mentioned to
be male. When the nursery is flooded, the

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:04.430
baby seems to be floating in that wood box.
The image was reminiscent of baby Moses being

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:08.240
sent down the river in a wood basket to survive
the Israelites.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:12.441
I also found the old couple scene to be significant.
The father takes his son to the river with

00:06:12.441 --> 00:06:16.071
him to show him how to survive on his own.
Then they come across the old couple. The

00:06:16.071 --> 00:06:20.550
woman is dead and the man gives himself up.
This is a symbolic passing of the torch from

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:24.730
old to new. The boy experiences a rite of
passage, and at the end of the movie, he'll

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:28.080
be expected to rise up and become the man
of the household.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:32.880
And I'm going to refer to the newspapers one
more time for another religious connotation.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:38.350
More then one publication refers to the aliens
as "angels of death" or "dark angels of destruction"

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:42.850
which could go back to the idea of the new
baby representing Moses and the angel of death

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:44.310
passing over him.

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:47.640
If you're interested in that kind of stuff,
go check out my Things You Missed on mother!

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:53.281
where I go much more in depth about the religious
symbolism from Aronofsky's latest flick. Just

00:06:53.281 --> 00:06:58.030
make sure you stay quiet, stay safe and stay
up to date on my new videos by subscribing

00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:04.290
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring
the deathbell for notifications and I'll see

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:07.650
you in the next one. Assuming we both survive.

